# Shared Worker Role skeleton.
#
# This file carries semantics, not bytes: it declares which invariants exist,
# which roles carry them, and how divergent the two runtimes currently are.
# It renders nothing. Every prose form lives in the role-local sources next to
# it, because the same invariant is worded differently in every role today.
#
# class:
#   shared   same meaning in both runtimes; wording differences are unfinished
#            normalization, not design
#   runtime  deliberately different because the runtimes differ; the intent
#            block states why
#   drift    differs with no runtime justification; awaiting the normalization
#            phase, which is blocked on the behavioural verification seam

id role.description
applies check-runner commit-writer log-summarizer repo-explorer
class drift
intent
Names the role, its reserved decisions and its routing preference over a
generic agent. The Codex form currently omits the cost-routing sentence and
the Git-state clause the Claude form carries. Nothing about Codex requires
that omission.
END

id git.no-mutation
applies check-runner commit-writer log-summarizer repo-explorer
class drift
intent
The role never mutates Git state: no staging, committing, pushing, rebasing,
and no writes to the index, refs, commits or remotes. All four roles carry
this, in four different wordings, for no reason other than history.
END

id checks.caller-named
applies check-runner
class shared
intent
Only the commands the caller named are run. The role never widens the batch.
END

id artifacts.tracked-source
applies check-runner
class shared
intent
Ordinary build and test artifacts may appear; tracked source may not. A check
that changes tracked source stops the batch.
END

id git.fingerprint
applies check-runner
class shared
intent
Tracked state is fingerprinted before and after the batch, and a changed
fingerprint is reported as a failure without restoring anything.
END

id evidence.per-check
applies check-runner
class shared
intent
Every check returns the same evidence shape, and a failing check is a task
result rather than a launch failure.
END

id evidence.check-cardinality
applies check-runner
class shared
intent
A check is one caller-named command, not an assertion hidden inside its
output.
END

id evidence.no-invention
applies check-runner
class shared
intent
Only observed output is reported as evidence; source-derived claims are
labelled as inference and counts are never invented.
END

id relay.target
applies check-runner repo-explorer
class shared
intent
Work the role may not do itself is relayed to one named sibling role, with
the minimum approved context.
END

id relay.nesting-limit
applies check-runner repo-explorer
class runtime
intent
Claude plugin subagents cannot spawn another subagent, so the relay must go
back through the primary. Codex allows exactly one nested hop. Same intent,
genuinely different mechanics.
END

id relay.child-boundary
applies check-runner repo-explorer
class runtime
intent
The child's permission boundary and the root's four-worker budget are
preserved. Codex additionally states minimum-context passing and no launch
retry, because only Codex actually has a child to launch.
END

id relay.trigger
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
The relay fires on an explicit verification request, or when the answer
depends on a runtime command passing rather than on file content.
END

id role.leaf
applies commit-writer log-summarizer
class shared
intent
A leaf role never dispatches another worker.
END

id boundaries.caller-decided
applies commit-writer
class shared
intent
Commit and PR boundaries are the caller's decision; the role only drafts text
for boundaries already fixed.
END

id input.caller-supplied
applies commit-writer
class shared
intent
The only inputs are the caller-supplied diff and the caller-supplied recent
commit subjects.
END

id message.why-not-what
applies commit-writer
class shared
intent
The commit message explains why, stays short, and does not restate the diff.
END

id pr.shape
applies commit-writer
class shared
intent
A PR title stays under 70 characters and the description is a few bullets,
not a file-by-file restatement.
END

id issue.linking
applies commit-writer
class shared
intent
The caller's issue-linking convention is followed, distinguishing an
auto-closing link from an epic link.
END

id output.contract
applies commit-writer
class shared
intent
Only the drafted message is returned; an empty diff or unclear intent is
reported instead of guessed.
END

id scope.exact-artifact
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
Only the exact caller-named artifact is read. Unrelated files, credentials,
environment files, branches and historical runs are out of scope.
END

id input.rejection
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
Binary, unknown-encoding, oversized, unscoped or potentially sensitive
unsanitized input is rejected rather than summarized.
END

id summary.root-causes
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
The summary covers root causes and important events.
END

id secrets.residual-scan
applies log-summarizer
class shared
intent
A clean residual scan is evidence that the installed rules ran, never proof
that no secret remains.
END

id scope.caller-repo
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
The answer stays inside the caller's repository scope.
END

id evidence.cited
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
Facts carry file and line provenance, unresolved uncertainty is stated, and
the commands used are reported.
END

id verification.reserved
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
Test, build and lint commands are reserved for the check-runner; exploration
inspects repository content only.
END

id decisions.none
applies repo-explorer
class shared
intent
The role makes no implementation or architecture decisions.
END
